# Avatar face photo (capture ↔ home)

Full write-up: `app/src/avatar/FACE_PHOTO.md`

## Invariant

**What is visible through the face hole at capture must be what fills the hole on the home avatar** (optional un-mirror after crop is OK; framing must not change).

## Do

- Keep the CameraView **hole-centered** and sized from the hole (`hole / CAPTURE_PREVIEW_SCALE`).
- Save the **center fraction** of that photo (`captureCenterHoleCrop`) — same region shown through the hole.
- Keep face-hole layout in **artwork space** (1024×1536); map with `contain` via `computeFaceHole` (same as `<Image resizeMode="contain" />`). The leathers cut-out is a **pixel circle** — re-measure with `python3 scripts/measure-face-holes.py` after art changes.
- Skip Align modal after **camera** capture; Align is for **library** picks only (hole-aspect crop, not forced square).
- Process the capture (do **not** use `skipProcessing` on Android) so front-camera `mirror` is baked in before crop/flip.
- On **web**, resolve crop size with `Image.getSize` (track settings lie) and **do not** flip after capture (preview mirror is CSS-only).

## Do not

- Reintroduce screen→photo **cover-fit mapping** (CSS scale / full-screen projection). It caused wrong home framing (partial face, offset head).
- Apply hole `%` as if the badge were filled edge-to-edge without `contain` letterboxing.
- Change leathers PNG size/aspect or hole cut-out without **re-measuring** art-space hole fractions and updating `DEFAULT_FACE_HOLE_LAYOUT`.

## Manual check after changes

Take photo with full face in hole → home avatar shows the same full face (not a zoomed corner / offset crop).
